  "skipped_target_dates": [],
  "methodology_note": "Each sample is the real Landsat Collection 2 Level-2 surface-reflectance scene closest to its target date, among up to the 8 lowest-cloud candidates in a widening +/-60/180/365 day window, whose QA_PIXEL band shows at least 70% of the local window clear of fill pixels (including Landsat 7's post-2003 SLC-off scan gaps), cloud, dilated cloud and cloud shadow: a scene-wide cloud_cover percentage says nothing about this one small window, so every candidate's own local window is checked directly instead of trusted on that number alone. Every read is anonymous and windowed directly from Microsoft Planetary Computer, never a full scene download. NDVI is computed from the real red/NIR reflectance after applying the USGS Collection 2 scale and offset, then thresholded to a 0..1 density value with the same formula at every date, so the samples are directly comparable across decades. No model was trained or run."
